--- redundant-lambda-parameter-parentheses.md ---
---
title: "redundant-lambda-parameter-parentheses"
rule: "redundant-lambda-parameter-parentheses"
category: "Style"
default: false
fix: "fixable_fix"
source: "crates/robusta_linter/src/rules/redundant_lambda_parameter_parentheses.rs"
---

<!-- This file is auto-generated by tasks/website_linter/src/rules/doc_page.rs. Do not edit it manually. -->

<RuleHeader />

Reports parentheses around one concise lambda parameter: `(value) ->
value` is `value -> value`.

JLS §15.27.1 defines the singleton concise forms `(x)` and `x` as
interchangeable. Typed, `var`, annotated, final, varargs, empty, and
multi-parameter lists stay parenthesized because they use different
grammar productions.

